{"schema":1,"function":"cauchy_ppf","description":"Cauchy distribution quantile function mu + b tan(pi (p - 1/2))","inputs":["mu","b","p"],"outputs":["y"],"points":186,"tolerance":{"rel":1e-13,"reason":"p is an exact double; a careful method forms T = tan(pi (p - 1/2)) within a few ulps (tan(pi d) with d = p - 1/2 exact (Sterbenz) for 1/4 <= p <= 3/4, -cot(pi p) below and cot(pi (1 - p)) above, 1 - p exact), and exactly -1, 0 and 1 at p = 1/4, 1/2 and 3/4; then mu + b T costs (|mu| + |b T|) / |mu + b T| ulps, at most about 8.8 on this grid where the quantile is not 0 (mu = -10, b = 1/4, p = 0.99; tested), 1e-15, and nothing where it is 0 (mu = -b, p = 3/4: T = 1 exactly). 1e-13 as for the other quantiles"},"grid":"(mu, b) in {(0, 1), (0, 2^-500), (0, 2^500), (-10, 1/4), (100, 8), (-2^1023, 2^1023)} x the gamma_ppf probabilities (p = 0, 5e-324, 1e-300, 1e-100, 1e-50, 1e-20, 1e-10, 1e-5, 1e-3, 0.01, 0.05, 0.1, 0.25, 0.4, 1/2 - 1e-10, 1/2, 1/2 + 1e-10, 0.6, 0.75, 0.9, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999, 1 - 1e-5, 1 - 1e-10, 1 - 1e-15 and 1), the doubles next to 1/2 (1/2 - 2^-54, 1/2 + 2^-53) and p = 1/8, 7/8; p = 0 and 1 are tagged pole (-inf and +inf), quantiles beyond the largest double are tagged overflow","mpmath":{"version":"1.4.1","dps":[50,100]},"scipy":{"version":"1.18.1","function":"scipy.stats.cauchy.ppf"},"numpy":"2.5.4","python":"3.13"}
